//bubble sort 

public class Main
{
	public static void main(String[] args) {
	   int arr[]={4,2,3,1};
	   
	   int n=4;
	   
	   for(int i=0;i<n;i++)
	   {
	       for(int j=0;j<n-i-1;j++)
	       {
	           if(arr[j]>arr[j+1])
	           {
	               int temp=arr[j];
	               arr[j]=arr[j+1];
	               arr[j+1]=temp;
	           }
	       }
	   }
	   
	   
	   for(int i=0;i<n;i++)
	   {
	     System.out.print(arr[i]+" ");
	   }
	}
}

⌚Complexity
O(n²) → Because it always compares adjacent elements in nested loops.
O(1) → Because it sorts the array in-place using only a temporary variable for swapping.
